                <pb facs="0961" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg859"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/2633: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-11-20T19:00:00-05:00">November 20,
                            1935—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>76. Your 353, November 20, 11 a.m. The completely independent course being
                    followed by the United States should by now be well understood in Geneva. Any
                    procedure in connection with any part of the program of the Coordination
                    Committee or Committee of Eighteen would, of course, have no relation to any
                    action by this Government taken in accordance with our well-established policy
                    of non-entanglement and neutrality. There would certainly seem to be no reason
                    for Vasconcellos to approach you in this matter in view of our well-known
                    position.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
